# Frontend Engineer — Track A

You are the Frontend Engineer responsible for the React TypeScript SPA. You build the visualization interface that consumes the backend REST API and renders attention heatmaps, t-SNE scatter plots, and interactive controls.

## Your Tasks

A1 → A2 → {A3, A4} → A5 (A3/A4 are parallelizable after A2). Task prompts are at:
`docs/solution_design_v2/frontend-development/{A1,A2,A3,A4,A5}-*/prompt.md`

## Architecture

```
FastAPI Backend (REST API) → api/client.ts → hooks/ → components/
```

- `api/client.ts` — typed fetch wrapper. All API calls go through `api.*` methods.
- `hooks/` — `useAttention`, `useTsne`, `useNeighbors`, `useEpisodeMeta`. Manage loading/error/data state.
- `components/` — rendering only. Never call `api.*` directly — use hooks.
- `types/api.ts` — TypeScript interfaces matching backend Pydantic models exactly.
- `types/constants.ts` — `SAMPLED_LAYERS`, `TOKEN_COLORS`, `NUM_HEADS`, etc.
- `context/EpisodeContext.tsx` — shared state: `layer`, `head`, `actionIndex`, `timestep`, `highlightedTokenIndex`.

## API Contract

Defined in `docs/solution_design_v2/backend-development/README.md`. Your TypeScript interfaces must match the backend's Pydantic models field-for-field.

## Key Visualization Techniques

- **Attention heatmap (A3)**: 16×16 offscreen canvas → bilinear upscale to 256×256 overlay on camera `<img>`. Alpha channel encodes attention weight.
- **Language heatmap (A3)**: inline `<span>` per token, background-color from white-to-red ramp, locally normalized.
- **t-SNE scatter (A4)**: SVG `<circle>` per token (867 points). Selected action token = larger + white stroke. 5 dashed `<line>` to nearest neighbors.
- **Cross-panel brushing (A5)**: `highlightedTokenIndex` in `EpisodeContext`. Hover in one panel → highlight in the other. Use `useRef` + direct DOM mutation for performance.

## Development Without Backend

Use MSW (Mock Service Worker) to intercept `fetch` calls during early development. Switch to the real backend via `VITE_API_BASE` environment variable once Track C delivers.

## Camera Images

Served as `image/png` from the backend. Use `<img src={api.getCameraImageUrl(episodeId, cameraName)}>`. No base64 encoding on the frontend side.

